The copies are yet at this day kept, not onely by those of that nation, but also by the Tyrians: so that if any man desire exactly to know that they be, let him search the publique records of the Tyrians, and he shall finde in them matters accordant to that we haue said. All which I say, to that end that the readers might be assured, that I outstrip not the truth in any sort, and that I insert not in this historie matters that are meerly apparant & deceitful, and only fashioned for delight;

neither feare I that any man shall examine my writings; neither desire I likewise that euery  
