All which I say, to that end that the readers might be assured, that I outstrip not the truth in any sort, and that I insert not in this historie matters that are meerly apparant & deceitful, and only fashioned for delight;

neither feare I that any man shall examine my writings; neither desire I likewise that euery  
                         man giue credit at the first sight to the same, or that I be held blamelesse in suffering my selfe any waies to vary or vnproperly dilate ought in this historie: but contrariwise if I cannot approoue the truth by demonstration, and sufficient testimonies, I desire not to be allowed. As soone as Salomon had receiued these letters from the King of the Tyr
